<title>ITALY: ALPINE SKIING - WOMEN'S COMBINED SLALOM RESULTS.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING - WOMEN'S COMBINED SLALOM RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>SESTRIERE, Italy 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of the women's</p>
<p>combined slalom at the Alpine skiing world championships on</p>
<p>Thursday (first leg 53 gates, second leg 53 gates, vertical drop</p>
<p>140 metres):</p>
<p>1. Morena Gallizio (Italy) one minute, 25.92 seconds</p>
<p>(44.13/41.79)</p>
<p>2. Marlies Oester (Switzerland) 1:26.89 (44.47/42.42)</p>
<p>3. Hilde Gerg (Germany) 1:28.22 (45.31/42.91)</p>
<p>4. Katja Seizinger (Germany) 1:28.27 (45.86/42.41)</p>
<p>5. Catherine Borghi (Switzerland) 1:28.28 (54.87/42.41)</p>
<p>6. Sibylle Brauner (Germany) 1:28.55 (45.73/42.82)</p>
<p>7. Renate Goetschl (Austria) 1:28.75 (46.21/42.54)</p>
<p>8. Anita Wachter (Austria) 1:29.64 (46.63/43.01)</p>
<p>9. Miriam Vogt (Germany) 1:29.72 (46.68/43.04)</p>
<p>10. Florence Masnada (France) 1:29.79 (46.99/42.80)</p>
<p>11. Marianne Kjoerstad (Norway) 1:30.10 (46.89/43.21)</p>
<p>12. Iveta Kohutova (Slovakia) 1:31.65 (47.83/43.82)</p>
<p>13. Michaela Dorfmeister (Austria) 1:32.47 (47.87/44.60)</p>
<p>14. Karolina Sedova (Czech Republic) 1:38.39 (50.87/47.52)</p>
<p>15. Petra Bartlova (Czech Republic) 1:38.54 (50.37/48.17)</p>
<p>16. Carola Calello (Argentina) 1:39.85 (50.85/49.00)</p>
<p>17. Anna Larionova (Russia) 1:45.25 (53.37/51.88)</p>
<p>18. Simona Pastinaru (Romania) 1:48.90 (55.76/53.14)</p>
<p>19. Svetlana Novikova (Russia) 1:52.56 (57.44/55.12)</p>
<p>Did not finish second run:</p>
<p>Maria Kvopkova (Slovakia)</p>
<p>Marie Joelle Clement (Canada)</p>
<p>Did not finish first run:</p>
<p>Pernilla Wiberg (Sweden)</p>
<p>Ingeborg Helen Marken</p>
